kernora-apps (1.1.27) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Screenshot works with several monitors: every monitor is captured on its
    own (KWin CaptureScreen) and gets its own selection overlay, a
    layer-shell surface pinned to that monitor (org.kde.layershell). Before,
    the active monitor's picture went into one fullscreen window that KWin
    put on another monitor, so the first screen seemed to jump to the
    second; KWin also ignores the screen a fullscreen window asks for, which
    is why the overlays are layer surfaces now. The selection and the
    toolbar follow the mouse; Screen takes the monitor the mouse is on.
  * What's new: screenshots with two monitors.

