kernora-apps (1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the everyday applications of Kernora OS in its
    Material 3 design, instead of KDE's.
  * Settings: network, Bluetooth, display and Night Light, sound,
    notifications, wallpaper and style (light or dark for the whole
    system), apps, battery and power, keyboard, mouse and touchpad,
    accessibility, security and privacy, account, date and time,
    language and region, updates, storage, about and legal information,
    with search; the systemsettings command is diverted to it.
  * Files, Text Editor, Photos, Media Player, Calculator and Screenshot.
  * Welcome at the first logins of an installed system.
  * Style: Material Design 1, 2 or 3 for the whole system, in Settings
    (Wallpaper & style) and as a step of Welcome, each choice drawn as a
    small window in that generation's look; org.kernora.system's
    Appearance switches the schemes, Plasma theme, Kvantum, window frames
    and panel together, and keeps the choice in ~/.config/kernorarc.
  * org.kernora.system, the Qt Quick module the applications use to read
    and change the system, with MprisPlayer: an application's MPRIS
    presence for the quick settings media card, the lock screen and media
    keys.
  * Media Player speaks MPRIS and shows the album's cover (from the file or
    a cover image in its folder).
  * Russian translations.
  * File chooser: every program's open, save and folder dialogs in
    Kernora's design instead of KDE's, as an xdg-desktop-portal backend
    (kernora-filechooser) built from Files' places, path bar and tiles:
    filters, several files, folders, a suggested name, replacing, new
    folders, the program's own choices. Qt programs (plasma-integration)
    and GTK programs are sent to the portal; a KWin rule keeps the window
    centred and above, as Qt programs on Wayland cannot name their window.
  * Settings and Welcome: light or dark and the Material generation as
    plain rows (a Dark theme switch and an Interface style choice; radio rows
    in Welcome) instead of illustrated cards; every Kernora live wallpaper is
    offered, with a still of its scene (Files.liveWallpapers(),
    Files.setLiveWallpaper(id)).
  * The web browser is LibreWolf: Welcome lists it among the apps, and
    About > Legal names it, with the copyright summary Kernora ships for it
    (/usr/share/kernora/copyright/librewolf), as its package has none.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
